decision: changes-requested

Three medium blockers remain:

- **N31 — Approval still implies closure before explicit close.** [review_bundle.go:3468](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3238950160/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:3468) returns an aggregate’s own approved verification immediately. That verification uses member lifecycle status to report `closed` at line 3739, without requiring its closeout receipt. An adopted `always` milestone can therefore disagree with `GetCloseoutState`, which correctly reports `CloseRequired=true`.
- **N32 — Exemption discards child failures.** [review_bundle.go:3510](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3238950160/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:3510) replaces the original verification and its blockers. A receipt checks composition and exit-gate identity, not current child approval. After a member loses approval, the exempt aggregate can still report `closed`; roadmap verification likewise checks child receipts rather than their current standing.
- **N33 — Some review readers still use transferred source stubs.** [review_plan.go:582](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3238950160/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_plan.go:582) selects components from the original member. [review_closeout.go:2555](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3238950160/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:2555) also reads that member’s lifecycle. A transferred source is `superseded`, so an approved aggregate can remain `ready-to-close` after its canonical destination and receipt satisfy closeout.

The closeout-policy tests passed in all three packages. The required artifact check exited 0; surface-check reported one target, 213 results and zero findings. Additional overlay probes could not run because the sandbox provides no writable temporary directory; the findings above rely on code inspection. The repository remains unchanged.

Rules applied: mixed Go/governance feature review; security, backend-go, documentation-style, delivery-evidence and knowledge-governance. No attestation or contribution was recorded.

